  "establishedCause": [
    "App composer-journal guard calls prepareSourceJournal, which performs readSourceDraft for every mounted thread before ordinary journalFlush.",
    "SourceWorkbench registers a second independent guard that also calls readSourceDraft for every owner, without any feature or recovery participation check.",
    "Both source reads call journalReadRecord, whose uncached/unstaged path opens IndexedDB. The retained fixture makes indexedDB.open synchronously throw IDB unavailable and never performs an authoring or source action.",
    "prepareEditorHandoff waits every guard and rejects if any fails. DesktopProvider converts that rejection to false and restores editing state."
  ],
  "evidenceLimits": [
    "The trace records the false acknowledgment, storage fault injection, successful disabled/recovery-alert assertions, 404 workbench reads and a successful edit.end command. It does not record which rejecting guard was selected first by Promise.allSettled.",
    "The ordinary fixture does not mock authenticated enabled:false. Its workbench catalogue and input reads return404. Do not label this as an executed host flag-off contract or installed desktop result.",
    "Accepted b4aa has journalFlush-only composer guard and prepareWorkspace. That source comparison establishes the added I/O path; no new accepted-base execution was performed.",
    "The other three failures are alert-role assertions assigned to root and are outside this repair."
  ],
  "rejectedShortcuts": [
    "Removing only App read leaves the SourceWorkbench guard rejection.",
    "Feature flag bypass could omit retained sources when new actions are disabled.",
    "journalGeneration alone ignores cold recovery, first CAS/Many until oncomplete, and independently recovered agents-pending.",
    "A broad catch on source/IDB failures could turn malformed/foreign data or failed owned writes into permission to close."
  ],
